title    Fixed Changes
tempo    92
beats    4
steps    4

voice pad   epiano vol=0.5 center=E4
voice kick  kick
voice snare snare
voice hat   hat vol=0.4
# Fingered electric bass, slightly short gate so the repeated rhythm stays
# articulated against the sustained pad instead of blurring into it.
voice bass  ebass vol=0.9 gate=0.85

pattern A
pad   | [Am7]--------------- | [D7]--------------- | [Gmaj7]--------------- | [Cmaj7]--------------- |
kick  | x... ..x. x... .... | % | % | % |
snare | .... x... .... x... | % | % | % |
hat   | x.x. x.x. x.x. x.x. | % | % | % |
# Bass intent: lock to the kick. Every bar uses the same rhythm, with notes on
# steps 1, 7 and 9 (the three kick hits) plus two eighth notes at the end of
# the bar. The root lands on beat 1 with the kick, the 5th answers the kick
# pickup on the "and" of beat 2, and a chord tone (3rd or 7th) sits on beat 3.
# The last eighth of each bar is a half-step approach into the next root
# (Eb->D, F#->G, B->C, G#->A), so the ii-V-I-IV in G walks smoothly and the
# loop back to Am7 is prepared. Range stays in E2-C3, under the pad (centered
# on E4) so the two never collide.
bass  | A2--- .. E2- G2--- E2- Eb2- | D2--- .. A2- C3--- A2- F#2- | G2--- .. D2- F#2--- A2- B2- | C3--- .. G2- E2--- G2- G#2- |

loop A
